cb16-builder-session
====================

The runner in lib/index.js is modelled on `@deepseek-ai/dsh-headless` from the
DeepSeek Harness distribution (MIT), which is the reference implementation of
the one-shot direct Agent driver. The session identity handling, resume
validation, fallback and machine-readable output are CB16 additions; the
turn-driving sequence (create/resume an Agent through the core registry, await
quiescence, append one user message, flush the session, print the final
assistant text and exit) follows that reference so the new path behaves like the
legacy one.

The startup plugin in lib/startup.js follows the command-line provider pattern of
`@deepseek-ai/dsh-headless/startup` for the same reason.

No third-party source outside the DeepSeek Harness distribution was copied. The
plug-in described in the task brief (ghbhiee/dsh-plugin-cli-session) was studied
for its pattern only - replace the startup/runner pair, inherit the rest - and
nothing from it was reused, including its sessionTag -> agentPreset design, which
CB16 deliberately rejects.
